::  name       mantra weave field count
::  shape      fields - int (@u32)
::  invariant  a Weave carries exactly three fields (lines - next_pos - next_run)
::  example    3
::  readers    Mantra - Glow Tend - Sur museum - Ashvini nest-only
::  nib        equinox-e204-mantra-tend-v0
::
::  Equinox e204 - Mantra M2 -- second Mantra structure pedestal in src/shape/.
::  Names Weave's field count from mantra/src/weave.rye: the append-only line
::  roster, the next position cursor, and the next run number. Pedestal only;
::  Rye still owns advance - current - Diff - Store.
::
::  Moved two to three on 20260907.182409, and it had been three since
::  20260907.173200. The count stood at two for a whole lap while the struct
::  declared `next_run`, because the field reader stopped at the doc comment
::  above it and the guard's pin agreed with that reading. Widening the reader
::  to read past `///` is what let this placard be wrong out loud.
+$  mantra-weave-field-count-shape
  $:  fields=@u32
  ==
